experiment: axiscollide
  instrument        axiscollide   trial seed 0000000001358bd9   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `gapwrite` showed B undoes A by restoring the neurons A
                    silenced. If that is the mechanism, retention should turn
                    on how much B's target requires A's AXIS to move -- not on
                    how far apart the two targets are.
  one account, two  opposite demands on the SAME neurons collide (`retain`,
  results           0.22); demands on DIFFERENT neurons coexist (`capacity`,
                    0.84). This tests whether that is one thing or two.

  THE ARMS (lesson A is always /i/, F1 320, F2 2500, taught as shipped)
    arm       F1     F2     dlogF1    dlogF2    asks of A's F1 write
    keep      320    2500   +0.000    +0.000    nothing
    f1-half   528    2500   +0.501    +0.000    reverse by 0.50
    f1-full   870    2500   +1.000    +0.000    reverse by 1.00
    f2-half   320    1516   +0.000    -0.500    nothing
    f2-full   320    920    +0.000    -1.000    nothing
